WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.346
Moonshot sold Kimi K3.1 Pro as K3 with more training.

00:00:04.346 --> 00:00:08.961
But its weight files hold one part the launch blog never mentions.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:12.768
Hi, I'm Bowline!

00:00:12.768 --> 00:00:15.237
Kimi K3.1 Pro is Moonshot's new flagship.

00:00:15.237 --> 00:00:17.706
The launch said: same model, more training.

00:00:17.706 --> 00:00:19.822
The weights say a little more.

00:00:21.758 --> 00:00:22.429
Chapter one.

00:00:22.429 --> 00:00:24.108
What carried over from K3.

00:00:28.883 --> 00:00:29.829
K3's architecture.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:35.975
Ninety-three layers, mostly Kimi Delta Attention, a linear attention with a constant-size state.

00:00:35.975 --> 00:00:39.757
Every fourth is a full-attention Gated MLA layer.

00:00:40.177 --> 00:00:42.468
Every layer feeds a mixture of experts.

00:00:42.468 --> 00:00:45.740
Each token goes to sixteen of eight hundred and ninety-six.

00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:53.063
The article read the header of all ninety-six weight shards in both repositories.

00:00:53.063 --> 00:00:55.942
K3 has four hundred ninety-seven thousand tensors.

00:00:56.362 --> 00:01:00.824
Every one is in K3.1 Pro, same name, same shape, same precision.

00:01:00.824 --> 00:01:04.542
But no shard's hash matches, so the weights moved everywhere.

00:01:04.962 --> 00:01:08.184
And there are a hundred and twenty new tensors, five in

00:01:08.184 --> 00:01:09.356
each of twenty-four layers.

00:01:09.776 --> 00:01:12.628
About a hundred and seventy-nine million new parameters.

00:01:12.628 --> 00:01:15.480
Exactly the gap between the two models' counts.

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:18.425
Chapter two.

00:01:18.425 --> 00:01:19.861
A sparse-attention indexer.

00:01:24.392 --> 00:01:28.671
The twenty-four new sets of tensors sit in the twenty-four full-attention layers.

00:01:28.671 --> 00:01:32.950
Each is a small indexer that scores every earlier token and passes

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:36.159
only the best two thousand and forty-eight to attention.

00:01:38.175 --> 00:01:39.906
Open one of those layers.

00:01:39.906 --> 00:01:44.059
The tensor names are DeepSeek's lightning indexer, and the model card calls

00:01:44.059 --> 00:01:45.444
the layer Gated DSA.

00:01:45.864 --> 00:01:50.092
Reading from the shapes: the indexer forms thirty-two small query heads from

00:01:50.092 --> 00:01:52.558
the query latent the layer already computes.

00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:57.151
It scores every earlier token, using one small key per token.

00:01:57.151 --> 00:01:58.289
No positional encoding.

00:01:58.709 --> 00:02:02.392
Only the top two thousand and forty-eight reach the real attention.

00:02:02.392 --> 00:02:05.070
Below that much context, nothing is left out.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:09.481
The repository ships no modelling code, so this is the article's reading

00:02:09.481 --> 00:02:11.476
of the tensors, not something run.

00:02:13.325 --> 00:02:16.814
In K3, each full-attention layer reads every earlier token.

00:02:16.814 --> 00:02:21.467
Those twenty-four layers are the only part whose cost grows with context.

00:02:21.887 --> 00:02:26.536
In K3.1 Pro, the indexer scores every earlier token first, with one

00:02:26.536 --> 00:02:29.635
small key each, a hundred and twenty-eight wide.

00:02:30.055 --> 00:02:33.738
Only the top two thousand and forty-eight reach the real attention.

00:02:33.738 --> 00:02:36.416
Below that much context, nothing is left out.

00:02:36.836 --> 00:02:41.512
At the full million-token window, the expensive attention reads five hundred and

00:02:41.512 --> 00:02:43.071
twelve times fewer entries.

00:02:43.071 --> 00:02:45.799
The indexer still scans everything, but cheaply.

00:02:46.219 --> 00:02:50.079
The price: if the indexer key is cached too, those layers store

00:02:50.079 --> 00:02:51.687
twenty-two percent more per token.

00:02:53.175 --> 00:02:53.961
Chapter three.

00:02:53.961 --> 00:02:55.926
More reinforcement learning, less said.

00:02:59.442 --> 00:03:03.446
K3 trained nine separate experts, then distilled them into one model.

00:03:03.866 --> 00:03:09.360
K3.1 Pro runs joint reinforcement learning across hundreds of domains, and strips

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.649
cyber data, even from mid-training.

00:03:13.175 --> 00:03:14.775
Start from the K3 checkpoint.

00:03:14.775 --> 00:03:16.375
The experts keep their shape.

00:03:16.795 --> 00:03:21.523
Most of the cost is generation: long agent runs against tools, in

00:03:21.523 --> 00:03:23.492
sandboxes across hundreds of domains.

00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:25.897
Every domain has its own reward.

00:03:25.897 --> 00:03:29.868
One buggy environment can teach the wrong thing, so Moonshot vets them

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:31.192
on a shared platform.

00:03:31.612 --> 00:03:33.352
Then update, and around again.

00:03:33.352 --> 00:03:36.831
The claim is that extra compute now pays off predictably.

00:03:38.883 --> 00:03:39.474
Chapter four.

00:03:39.474 --> 00:03:40.953
Does the launch hold up?

00:03:46.758 --> 00:03:52.071
On Terminal-Bench four point oh, K3.1 Pro nearly ties Claude Opus five point five.

00:03:52.491 --> 00:03:57.064
It leads on agentic, tool-using work like OfficeQA Pro, and trails on

00:03:57.064 --> 00:03:58.589
closed-book knowledge and cyber.

00:04:00.092 --> 00:04:05.208
The sixty-five percent drop is this internal stress test, checked claim by claim.

00:04:05.208 --> 00:04:07.176
GPT-6 Astra is still lower.

00:04:08.733 --> 00:04:10.506
The article checked the launch claims.

00:04:11.044 --> 00:04:16.298
Against the proprietary models, K3.1 Pro is ahead or tied on sixteen

00:04:16.298 --> 00:04:18.925
of forty-five rows, mostly agentic ones.

00:04:19.345 --> 00:04:23.770
Counted per response, the hallucination drop is fifty-seven point six percent.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:27.316
And a viral demo's tokens and price cannot both be right

00:04:27.316 --> 00:04:28.453
at Moonshot's own rates.

00:04:30.142 --> 00:04:34.243
A new flagship can be mostly the same network, trained much harder

00:04:34.243 --> 00:04:36.635
afterwards, with one indexer for long context.

00:04:38.733 --> 00:04:43.170
Same experts, a new attention indexer, much more reinforcement learning, and a

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:44.649
lead on agentic work.

00:04:44.649 --> 00:04:45.758
Thanks for watching!

00:04:46.178 --> 00:04:48.296
Every source is in the full article.

00:04:48.296 --> 00:04:48.901
I'm Bowline.

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:49.204
Bye!
